                    DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION

                             FACT SHEET


PRODUCT NAME:  GIGAswitch/ATM System Firmware V1.4


OVERVIEW:  

ATM Forum-compliant LAN Emulation (LANE), plus added-value LANE 
features from Digital, have been added to the GIGAswitch/ATM system, 
a high-performance ATM switch especially for use in LAN backbones 
and high performance workgroups.  LAN Emulation was introduced in 
Firmware V1.3. Enhancements to LAN Emulation and support for UNI 3.1 
are added in Firmware V1.4.

The GIGAswitch/ATM system supports Permanent Virtual Circuits and 
Switched Virtual Circuits as well as Constant Bit Rate (CBR), 
Variable Bit Rate (VBR) traffic, and Available Bit Rate (ABR) 
traffic.  Through FLOWmaster flow control, the system eliminates 
cell loss for ABR traffic, providing a robust network for bursty 
data traffic.  The GIGAswitch/ATM can be managed by any 
SNMP-compliant network management application, including POLYCENTER 
NetView and HP OpenView.  The switch can also be managed through an 
out-of-band management interface via a Telnet session or by 
Digital's HUBwatch, a Graphical User Interface (GUI)-based SNMP 
network management application.  The firmware upgrade is downline-
loadable.

The GIGAswitch/ATM system supports up to fifty-two 155 Mbps 
SONET/SDH multimode fiber and/or single-mode fiber ports, using a 
10.4 Gbps switch fabric.  Later, support will be extended to other 
media and to T1/E1, T3/E3 and 622 Mbps SONET/SDH.  


