              DIGITAL BUILDS ON ITS LEADERSHIP POSITION
              IN PCI STORAGE AND CLUSTERING TECHNOLOGY


       New StorageWorks Adapter Allows Alpha Customers To Add
   High-Performance PCI-based Systems To Their Cluster Environment



MAYNARD, Mass., February 21, 1996 -- Building on its leadership 
position in PCI storage and clustering technology, Digital Equipment 
Corporation's Storage Business Unit today announced the new 
StorageWorks CIPCA adapter.  With the CIPCA adapter, AlphaServer 
users now have the ability to attach CI-based storage to PCI-based 
AlphaServer and Digital systems.  With the CIPCA adapter, 
AlphaServer users now have the ability to attach PCI-based 
AlphaServers to the CI-based storage subsystems used in their 
VMScluster environments.

     The CIPCA adapter, designed in a joint technology partnership 
between Digital and CMD Technology of Irvine CA, combines "best of 
breed" technology with the award-winning, modular/scalable design of 
the StorageWorks product line.  CIPCA supports the StorageWorks HSC 
and HSJ RAID array controllers, providing PCI-based systems with 
scalable performance, capacity and availability.  The StorageWorks 
adapter family delivers ready access to both high-performance 
storage controllers and a multitude of industry-standard SCSI 
devices, opening the door to substantial expansion storage, the most 
popular levels of RAID, high performance backups, and more effective 
storage solutions.

     "With the heightened performance of Alpha systems and servers, 
storage availability and accessibility is becoming increasingly 
critical," said Ed McCarren, Digital platform marketing manager for 
Digital's Storage Business Unit.  "With the integration of the CIPCA 
adapter, customers have the ability to add high-performance 
PCI-based systems to their cluster environment, resulting in 
significantly faster throughput, higher availability and reduced 
storage management costs.  Customers can now add the latest high-
performance PCI-based AlphaServers to their cluster environment, 
taking advantage of the high availability, performance, and 
management benefits of VMSclustering."

     Bruce Lambertos, director of sales for CMD Technology, said, 
"The new CIPCA adapter demonstrates the ongoing commitment from 
Digital and CMD Technology to bring new emerging technology like the 
PCI bus, into Digital's industry-leading cluster solution."

Availability

     The StorageWorks CIPCA adapter ranges in price from $12,095 - 
$16,300.  StorageWorks products for Digital platforms and operating 
environments are available through authorized distributors, from the 
Digital sales force, and through DECdirect and the ESTORE.  For more 
information about Digital's complete line of StorageWorks products, 
call 1-800-STORWORK (1-800-786-9675) or visit 
http://www.storage.digital.com/ on the World Wide Web.

     The StorageWorks product line is a comprehensive family of 
disk, tape and optical storage subsystems, offering modular, 
competitively-priced, industry-standard solutions in customizable 
desktop, deskside, departmental and datacenter enclosures.  
StorageWorks products are available on multiple operating systems 
and hardware platforms, including Digital, Hewlett-Packard, IBM and 
Sun workstations and servers, and Novell and Windows NT 
environments.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha Platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
