               DIGITAL EQUIPMENT CORPORATION ANNOUNCES
                   NEW HEAD OF INVESTOR RELATIONS


MAYNARD, Mass., February 26, 1996 -- Patrick J. Spratt has been 
named vice president for Investor Relations at Digital Equipment 
Corporation, Vincent J. Mullarkey, vice president and chief 
financial officer, announced today.

     Spratt, 48, who previously was vice president for business 
strategy in Digital's Accounts Business Unit, replaces Robert E. 
Hult who recently was named vice president, controller and 
operations for Digital's new Connectivity Software Business Unit.

     "Pat brings an extensive knowledge of Digital's business 
operations and the computer industry to this role, and has the 
business and communications skills required to maintain strong and 
stable investor relationships for Digital," Mullarkey said.

     Spratt has held a number of senior positions during his 22 
years at Digital, including vice president for business operations 
for the Computer Systems Division, vice president for engineering 
operations and finance, and software business manager.

     Prior to joining Digital, Spratt was employed by the Xerox 
Corporation. He holds a bachelor's degree in mathematics from Boston 
College and a master's degree in business administration from Boston 
University.  

