                 DIGITAL DELIVERS FAST ETHERNET HUB
                  FOR SMALL OFFICES AND WORKGROUPS


MAYNARD, Mass., February 26, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation
today introduced a low-cost Fast Ethernet hub for small offices and 
workgroups that need optimum response time from powerful 
applications.  Designed specifically to support workgroups running 
bandwidth-intensive applications such as client/server software, 
CAD/CAM, graphics or financial modeling, the EtherWORKS Hub 8TX is 
an 8-port, 100 Mb/s Fast Ethernet plug-and-play solution priced at 
$1,595. It is available immediately.

     The EtherWORKS Hub 8TX supports up to 8 workstations, PCs, and 
servers or can be connected with another EtherWORKS Hub 8TX to 
support up to 14 users.  Its compact desktop design simplifies 
installation.  Front-panel LED indicators provide vital network 
information including power, port utilization, collision rates, 
partition status, and link/traffic status.  

     To minimize performance disruption, the EtherWORKS Hub 8TX 
offers several smart features including auto-partitioning to isolate 
problem ports quickly, auto-polarity detection to recognize and 
adjust cable assemblies for correct polarity, and auto-jabber lock-
up to automatically stop the transmission of abnormal Ethernet 
frames that could cause data loss for network users.

     The EtherWORKS Hub 8TX interoperates with other products in 
compliance with the IEEE 802.3u 100Base-TX standard, including 
Digital's Fast EtherWORKS PCI 10/100 network interface cards.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms,
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete
