           DIGITAL ANNOUNCES PRICING AND AVAILABILITY FOR
       PENTIUM(R) 150MHz and 166MHz COMMERCIAL DESKTOP SYSTEMS


         Reduces Prices Up to 16% on Selected Desktop Models


MAYNARD, Mass., January 31, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced pricing and availability for its new 150MHz and 
166MHz Pentium processor-based commercial desktop systems, which 
were introduced earlier this month.  The new Intel(R) processors are 
available in several models within Digital's Celebris XL, Celebris 
GL and Venturis commercial desktop families.  At the same time, the 
company announced price reductions of up to 16 percent on selected 
commercial desktop models.  The new models, as well as the price 
reductions, are effective immediately in the U.S.

     "With todays announcement, Digital not only offers the latest 
in Intel Pentium processor technology, but continues our leadership 
role in helping customers make the transition from 486 to Pentium 
processing", said Raymond Weadock, vice president and general 
manager, Americas for Digital's Personal Computer business. 

Latest Pentium Processor Technology Shipping in Volume 

     Joining the industry's fastest personal workstation family are 
the new Celebris XL 5150 and Celebris XL 5166 models and a dual-
processor Celebris XL 5166 model. Combined with Windows NT, Digital's 
personal workstation family provides users of technical and compute-
intensive applications a combination of workstation-class performance 
and shrink-wrapped applications, with the look, feel and pricing of 
a PC.

     Celebris XL models feature 16MB RAM, 256/512K cache, 1GB SCSI 
hard drive, Matrox Millennium graphics card (or an AccelGraphics 
AG300, depending on configuration), 4X CD-ROM, and Digital's 
ClientWORKS network and asset management software.  The Celebris XL 
5150 is priced at $4,329 U.S.; the Celebris XL 5166 is priced at 
$4,579 U.S.; and the dual-processor Celebris XL 5166 is priced at 
$5,929 U.S.

     Digital's award-winning Celebris GL PCs, designed from the 
start to be performance desktop systems, offer advanced business 
users a potent combination of performance, flexibility and 
ease-of-use, winning PC Magazine's December 1995 Editors' Choice 
Award.  Packaged in short tower configurations, the Celebris GL 
family is ideal for fast-response, demanding business and analytical 
applications.

     Celebris GL models feature integrated, best-of-breed 
componentry, including 16MB EDO memory, 256 pipeline burst cache, 
Intel Triton FX chipset, PCI bus master Enhanced-IDE, Matrox 
Millennium graphics card, 4X CD-ROM, and Digital's ClientWORKS.  The 
Celebris GL 5150 is priced at $3,819 U.S; the U.S. price for the 
Celebris GL 5166 is $4,169.

     Added today to the Venturis value line are the new Venturis 
5150 and Venturis 5166 systems, which are available in both slimline 
and full-profile models.  Easy to use, service and manage, Digital's 
Venturis systems are designed to optimize productivity for 
enterprise computing users while offering exceptional price/
performance.

     Venturis models include 8MB RAM, 256 secondary cache, 630MB, 
845MB or 1.2GB IDE hard disk drives (depending on configuration), 
and Digital's ClientWORKS.  The U.S. price for the Venturis 5150 is 
$2,429; the Venturis 5166 is priced at $2,829 U.S.

Affordable Prices for the Desktop

     Continuing to support its corporate customers as they make the 
transition to Pentium technology, Digital announced significant 
price reductions across its entire commercial desktop line.  The 
price reductions range up to 16 percent and are applicable on 
selected models in the Digital Celebris XL, Celebris GL and Venturis 
product families.  

     Price cuts taken in the Celebris XL line range from the 
Celebris XL 5100, which now lists for $3,529 U.S., a reduction of 
$210; to the Celebris XL 5133, which now lists for $3,879 U.S., a 
drop of $550.  The Celebris XL 6150 Pentium ProTM processor-based 
system is priced at $5,449 U.S., a $100 price drop.  Digital's 
PowerGrade upgrade options also have been reduced by $100 - $250 
U.S., depending on the upgrade.

     Reductions in the slimline and short tower models of the 
Celebris GL line range from the Celebris GL 5100, which now lists 
for $3,019 U.S., a drop of $230; to the Celebris GL 5133ST, now 
listed at $3,619 U.S., a reduction of $430.

     The slimline and full-profile price cuts in the Venturis line 
range from the Venturis 575, which now lists for $1,479 U.S., a 
reduction of $120; to the Venturis 5133FP, now listed at $2,479 
U.S., a price cut of $370.

