                DIGITAL DELIVERS POLYCENTER NETWORKER
                 SAVE AND RESTORE TO MACINTOSH USERS


            POLYCENTER NetWorker Provides Macintosh Users
         With Significant Performance and Productivity Gains


MAYNARD, Mass., February 1, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced new Macintosh client support for POLYCENTER 
NetWorker Save and Restore, Digital's implementation of Legato 
System's industry-leading NetWorker product.  POLYCENTER NetWorker 
Save and Restore Macintosh Client Kit, Version 1.0, is the first 
network backup product for client/server environments that empowers 
networked Macintosh users with the option to backup or recover files 
or directories without administrator intervention.  Now, Macintosh 
users can benefit from significant gains in performance and reduced 
storage management costs by investing in the most comprehensive
network storage management solution available.

     "Digital's NetWorker is now meeting the increasing need for 
high-end robust storage in Macintosh environments, in addition to 
the needs of users in a broad range of platforms," said Peter 
George, Digital Equipment's director for Storage Software.  
"NetWorker for the Macintosh environment is unmatched in offering 
clients the highest-performing storage management solution by 
enabling clients to completely consolidate their backup strategy."

NetWorker for Macintosh Client Kit, Version 1.0

     The NetWorker for Macintosh Client Kit, Version 1.0, offers 
high performance at a low cost through a full range of features:

     * 	consolidated backup strategy through the use of one single 
        solution,

     * 	maintenance of different versions of the same file without 
        using excessive disk space,

     * 	direct access to the server for each client using MacTCP, a 
        faster alternative that out performs AppleTalk 10 to 1,

     * 	parallelism which allows multiple data servers and other 
        clients to send files to media simultaneously while the 
        parallel restore feature allows multiple files to be 
        recovered from media simultaneously,

     * 	centralized storage in one autoloader, instead of many small 
        servers,

     * 	scheduled backup of Macintosh computers at predefined 
        intervals to Mac OS Servers and MacTCP=AE,

     * 	full, incremental and eleven levels of differential backup 
        for up to 16 Macintosh computers, which can be backed up 
        simultaneously to a single NetWorker server.

Availability and Ordering

     POLYCENTER NetWorker Client Kit for Macintosh Version 1.0, 
QA-XYXAF-H8, developed by Digital Equipment Corporation's Storage 
Business Unit, is now available for $1,500.  Kits are also available 
for UNIX, PC, NT and NetWare clients for $1,500 each.  Products are 
available through DECdirect, Digital's business partners and local 
Digital sales offices.  For more information about Digital's 
complete line of hardware and software products, call 1-800-STORWORK 
(1-800-786-7967) or visit http://www.storage.digital.com/ on the 
World Wide Web.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha Platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
