     DIGITAL ANNOUNCES COMPREHENSIVE INTERNET SOLUTION PACKAGES


       Bundled Hardware, Software & Services For The Internet


MAYNARD, Mass., February 5, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced a comprehensive offering of four robust Internet 
Solution Packages to provide Internet-focused businesses and 
corporate users with bundled packages of hardware, software and 
services designed to meet a wide scope of business needs related to 
the Internet.

     With the hardware and software pre-configured in a range of 
prices, these packages are then customizable with services to meet 
the specific needs of clients to help them begin or expand 
operations on the Internet in the shortest possible time at the most 
competitive cost with the greatest understanding and benefit.

     Strongly supporting Digital's comprehensive Internet Solution 
Packages approach is Allen Weiner, Principal Analyst for Online 
Strategies at Dataquest, who stated that "for today's entrepreneur 
looking for an Internet solution, too many options present a piecemeal 
approach which requires integrating products whose architectures aren't 
inherently compatible.

     "Digital's Internet Solution Packages offer high-end users with 
robust applications - as well as those looking to dip their toes 
into new Internet waters - a one-stop, integrated hardware, software 
and services approach which makes being part of the online 
revolution a worry-free step," Weiner added.

The four Internet Solution Packages announced by Digital today are:

     INTERNET SERVICE PROVIDER (ISP) SOLUTION PACKAGE --- 

     Designed to provide prospective and existing Internet service 
     providers with a robust, integrated, production-level solution 
     for launching or expandingan ISP business. Configured to 
     support 2,500 to 5,000 subscribers, this package is a modular, 
     easily scalable building block that will support a minimum of 
     250 concurrent users from both dial-in or ISDN connections. It 
     will allow ISP's with an Internet connection to get up, running 
     and selling services without having to integrate an array of 
     complex networking technologies from multiple vendors.

     Priced at $169,900, this package is available worldwide and is 
     geared for the next generation of ISP's that will need to 
     compete on performance, accessible services, and high 
     availability. Included in the basic package are:  Digital's 
     rackmounted AlphaServer 1000; systems for managing customer 
     accounts; Web hosting; DNS; news feeds; and integrated 
     authentication and billing software. Services are included to 
     customize the solution to fit in either a start-up operation or 
     an existing environment. The basic package would need to be 
     augmented with a choice of industry-leading network access 
     products at additional cost. Options for systems designed for a 
     larger number of subscribers, higher-level security, and high 
     availability may also be ordered.

     Service Provider Solution Customer Comment: "Our customers are 
     telling us that they want an Internet Service Provider that 
     offers toll-free access to Internet-based services. Digital's 
     consulting and integration services, combined with its Internet 
     experience, allow us to meet that demand quickly and 
     effectively through a state-of-the-art network," said Ronald 
     E. Spears, Vice President of Telecommunications, Citizens 
     Utilities, Stamford, Connecticut.

     INTERNET INFORMATION DISTRIBUTION SOLUTION PACKAGE ---                

     Designed for manufacturers and distributors of complex 
     industrial products that want to use the World Wide Web to 
     distribute product information such as catalogs, drawings, 
     specifications, maintenance notices, etc. to their OEM 
     customers, dealers, and end-users, this package combines the 
     power of Digital's AlphaServer systems with features such as 
     rackmount design, clustering, and extensive consulting services 
     to create an industrial-strength Web server for mission-
     critical applications.

     With prices ranging from $60,500 on the low-end solution to 
     $218,100 on the high-end solution, this package is available 
     worldwide and - depending on customer needs - could include: 
     Digital's AlphaServer 400 or the rackmounted AlphaServer 1000 
     system; bundled Internet search and retrieval software such as 
     FTP, Gopher and WAIS; optional Web publishing software; and a 
     wide range of custom consulting, design and implementation 
     services from Digital.

     Information Distribution Solution Customer Comment: "Toys R Us 
     has recently implemented a Web site based upon Digital's 
     AlphaServer and systems integration services. We are very 
     pleased with the traffic that has been associated with the 
     site, and equally pleased with the support which Digital has 
     provided to us during the implementation," said Matt Lombardi, 
     Vice President of Information Technology, Toys R Us, Rochelle 
     Park, New Jersey).

     INTERNET COLLABORATION SOLUTION PACKAGE --- 

     Designed for users interested in workgroup collaboration, this 
     package allows customers, partners, and suppliers to share 
     information, notes files, discussion groups, and other 
     collaborative efforts seamlessly across internal (Intranet) and 
     external (Internet) networks.

     With prices ranging from $55,100 on the low-end solution to 
     $69,630 on the high-end solution, this package is available 
     worldwide and - depending on customer needs - could include: 
     Digital's AlphaServer system and Workgroup Web Forum software; 
     optional use of Digital's tunneling products; other publicly 
     available software; and custom services from Digital such as 
     consulting and training.

     Collaboration Solution Customer Comment: "Xerox is continually 
     seeking ways of enhancing the effectiveness of our work teams. 
     Since today's trend is for those work teams to be scattered 
     across the country or around the world, and to involve 
     universities and other companies, we are especially interested 
     in using the Internet and World Wide Web to enable close 
     information sharing and collaboration. Digital's Collaboration 
     Solution was the only system that came close to our needs. 

     The combination of Digital's Workgroup Web Forum software and 
     video-ready Alpha workstations with Xerox Liveboards allowed us 
     to reap the benefits of Web-based remote collaboration. Our 
     teams are delighted by their ability to share information, hold 
     discussions and work effectively with their colleagues inside 
     and outside of Xerox in a secure manner using the ubiquitous 
     and convenient medium of the Internet," said Dr. Gregory Zack, 
     Manager, Design Research Institute, Joseph P. Wilson Center for 
     Research and Technology, Xerox Corporation, Ithaca, New York.

     INTERNET MERCHANT SOLUTION PACKAGE --- 

     Designed for customers that want to operate an electronic 
     storefront to trade goods or services and accept orders and 
     credit-card payments over the Internet, this package is based 
     on a software product and architecture from Digital partner, 
     Open Market, Inc. of Cambridge, Massachusetts, a leading 
     provider of business software for the Internet. Features of 
     this package include the handling of financial transactions, 
     order taking and payments, credit card transactions, sales tax 
     processing, and other purchasing and distribution tasks over 
     the Internet.

     With prices ranging from $95,790 on the low-end solution to 
     $160,400 on the high-end solution, this package is currently 
     available in the United States only and - depending on customer 
     needs - could include: Digital's AlphaServer 400 or the 
     rackmounted AlphaServer 1000 system; Open Market's Merchant 
     Solution software; and custom Internet services from Digital.

     Merchant Solution Customer Comment: "Open Market's business 
     software for the Internet has enabled us to turn the Internet 
     into an effective business tool by broadening our reach to 
     small businesses. Through our Small Business Service, companies 
     can browse through our wealth of resources and purchase 
     articles on an as-needed basis. This gives small businesses 
     access to vital information for a fraction of the traditional 
     cost," said Patrick Toner, Director of Distribution Programs, 
     LEXIS-NEXIS, Dayton, Ohio.

     "Our goal is to make it easy for our customers to reap the 
benefits of doing business on the Internet by offering these unique, 
industrial-strength Internet Solution Packages," said Rose Ann 
Giordano, Vice President of Digital's Internet Business Group. 

     "While all other vendors in this marketplace are still focused 
on selling individual components or services, Digital is the only 
vendor that has put together customizable, integrated solution 
packages for the ever-expanding range of businesses and 
organizations now using the Internet. They provide tremendous 
operational benefits for Internet customers," she added.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated 
worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
