                 DIGITAL APPOINTS INACOM CORPORATION
                  AS ITS NEWEST PC CHANNEL PARTNER


MAYNARD, Mass., February 6, 1996 - Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced Inacom Corp. of Omaha, Neb. as its newest PC channel 
partner in the Americas.  Inacom will sell Digital's complete line 
of Intel-based PC products, including the Digital HiNote family of 
mobile computers targeted at sales automation applications; 
Digital's Venturis and Celebris commercial desktop PCs; the Celebris 
XL personal workstation family; and Digital's powerful Prioris PC 
servers.

     Inacom will give Digital an even broader reach into the 
corporate market, where we are traditionally very strong. said Ken 
Wyrick, vice president of channel sales for Digital's PC business in 
the U.S..  Inacom's network of 1,300 reseller locations and its 50 
company-owned branches will expand the availability of Digital PCs 
across the country.

     We're very pleased to enter into this agreement with Digital 
for many reasons. said Dan Kemp, Inacom's vice president of product 
marketing.  Our customers will benefit by having a wider range of 
desktop, mobile, and server products from which to choose.
Digital Prioris PC server products offer excellent scalability and 
expandability, as well as exceptional price/performance, which helps 
ensure significant investment protection for our customers.  The 
company offers an outstanding suite of management software, which 
delivers industry-leading levels of manageability and usability.  
And all of Digital's products have a great reputation for quality 
and worldwide customer service.

     Inacom Corporation is a global leader in helping business 
customers realize the full potential of information technology.  
Inacom provides technology management services which enable 
customers to integrate computer and communications systems form 
leading technology companies.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry- 
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
