              DIGITAL SHIPS DATA CENTER SCHEDULING TOOL
              FOR WINDOWS NT, UNIX AND OpenVMS SYSTEMS


       ... unique client/server architecture is scalable from
                 the workgroup to the enterprise...


MAYNARD, Mass., February 13, 1996 -- Digital Equipment Corporation 
today announced immediate availability of POLYCENTER Scheduler for 
Digital UNIX, which incorporates a three-tier architecture which is 
unique among data center scheduling products and provides 
scalability from desktops to enterprise systems.

     The flexible client/server/agent architecture of POLYCENTER 
Scheduler supports multivendor systems.  A software agent runs on 
each system on which jobs are scheduled.  Agents are available for 
Windows NT, Sun OS, HP-UX, Digital UNIX, OpenVMS VAX, and OpenVMS 
Alpha systems.  The  server software runs on Digital UNIX systems 
and contains the data repository  and central processing functions.

     The client software can run on any Digital UNIX system on the 
network.  It is the only scheduling product that enables systems 
personnel to schedule and execute production jobs from a single 
network location.  From one console, administrators can monitor data 
center tasks such as payroll, backup, and manufacturing resource 
planning.

     Systems programmer/project manager Kurt Carlson of the 
University of Alaska selected POLYCENTER Scheduler.  According to 
Carlson, "It has allowed us to completely automate many systems 
management functions as well as the normal job scheduling workload." 
He adds, "The ability of a Scheduler server to support multiple 
hosts has also proven invaluable as we have moved from a single 
monolithic mainframe environment to multiple distributed hosts."

     The new POLYCENTER Scheduler software boasts the most 
comprehensive set of features for reducing system administration 
costs.  Automatic load balancing optimizes system use by selecting 
the least used systems for running jobs. Jobs may initiate according 
to a schedule or initiation can be dependent upon completion of 
other jobs.  Job prioritization can restrict systems to run 
particular jobs during specified time periods.  The failover and 
recovery capabilities ensure completion of jobs by automatically 
restarting failed jobs on different systems.

     Pricing for POLYCENTER Scheduler for Digital UNIX server 
software starts at $3,000.  Client software is $1127, and agent 
software pricing starts at $225.  Additional information is 
available from Digital's POLYCENTER web page at 
http://www.digital.com/info/polycenter.

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open  
client/server solutions from personal computing to integrated  
worldwide information systems.  Digital's scalable Alpha platforms, 
storage, networking, software and services, together with industry-
focused solutions from business partners, help organizations compete 
and win in today's global marketplace.
