   DIGITAL JOINS WITH THE WASHINGTON POST, ABC NEWS AND NEWSWEEK
       TO PUT REAL TIME ELECTION RESULTS AND ANALYSIS ON LINE


Digital's Alpha Technology Powers Potential Record-Setting Web Site


WASHINGTON, D.C., Feb. 13, 1996 -- Real time election results 
and analysis are now available on the World Wide Web. Digital 
Equipment Corporation is providing the technology solution to 
launch the ElectionLine World Wide Web site from The Washington 
Post, ABC News and Newsweek.  ElectionLine, located at 
http://www.ElectionLine.com, delivers original political and 
election coverage each day plus news and analysis throughout the 
1996 election year.

     "ElectionLine builds on the innovative technology  developed 
by Digital in 1994 for the California Election Internet Web site," 
said Rose Ann Giordano, vice president of Digital's Internet 
Business Group.  "Digital's high performance, 64-bit Alpha 
architecture enables lightening-fast delivery of real time 
information to vast numbers of people around the world.  Digital, 
in partnership with ElectionLine, is providing an unprecedented 
opportunity, enabling a more-informed and engaged electorate." 

     ElectionLine covers daily campaign events, provides 
comprehensive information on candidates and issues, commentary and 
analysis, and real-time coverage of election results.  There also 
will be interactive forums, using Digital's Workgroup Web Forum 
software, enabling the public to discuss the issues and provide 
their views.

     "This project demonstrates Digital's ability to provide a 
total solution for complex Internet World Wide Web projects. We are 
using state-of-the-art 64-bit Alpha technology and systems 
integration expertise in  workgroup computing and network security 
in an Internet client/server environment," said Rick Distasio, 
Digital's Systems Integration vice president in the Washington 
region."

     "Technically, this is huge," said Ralph Terkowitz, vice 
president of technology  for the Washington Post Company.   
"Digital enables us to host a large volume of simultaneous users 
ensuring that ElectionLine is always accessible.  This technology 
allows us to present the news through a combination of video, audio 
and text.  Digital is part of an incredibly ambitious content 
effort."

     ElectionLine is supported by the design expertise and 
navigational technologies of Digital's partners Persimmon IT and 
Personal Library Software, Inc. 

     Persimmon IT, worked with Digital to design the ElectionLine 
Web site so that visitors can easily navigate among the chat rooms, 
breaking news, live events and myriads of searchable databases 
offered by participating news organizations and hyperlinked sites 
throughout the Internet.  

     Personal Library Software, Inc. (PLS) provides the search 
engine technology used for the ElectionLine site.  Known for its 
continuous updating and handling of massive databases, the PLS 
engine permits instantaneous searching and has been deployed here 
to make it easy for the user to focus quickly on the date, 
reporter, candidate, source, media type or issues of interest.  

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions from personal computers to integrated 
worldwide information systems.  Digital's Intel and Alpha 
platforms, storage, networking, software and services, together 
with industry-focused solutions from business partners, help 
organizations compete and win in today's global marketplace.  
More information is available at http://www.digital.com/info/internet/.
