                 DIGITAL AGAIN DOMINATES AIM HOT IRON AWARDS  

         
            ... 11  awards are the most ever by a single vendor ...
         

SAN FRANCISCO -- February 14, 1996 -- Demonstrating the 
superior customer value of its UNIX-based servers, 
workstations and PCs, Digital Equipment Corporation has again 
taken top honors in the latest performance and 
price/performance benchmarks conducted by AIM Technology, a 
leading independent performance testing service. 

     In announcing results of its testing at UniForum '96 here 
today, AIM Technology presented to Digital representatives 11 
AIM 1996 Hot Iron Awards, far more than any other vendor. No 
other vendor has ever collected as many honors from AIM in a 
single round of Hot Iron Awards. 

     The Digital systems recognized by AIM include AlphaServer 
systems and AlphaStation workstations based on Digital's 
industry-leading 64-bit RISC-based Alpha microprocessors and 
64-bit Digital UNIX operating system, and Digital's premier 
Prioris Intel and UNIX based PC servers. 

     Digital's Hot Iron Awards for 1996 are: 
         
     o   Best Performer, General Workstation Mix, priced under 
         $25,000: 

              DEC 3000 Model 600

     o   Best Performer, General Workstation Mix, $25,000 and 
         over: 

              AlphaStation 600 5/300

     o   Best Price/Performance Throughput, File Server Mix, 
         $25,000 to $49,000: 

              Prioris ZX 5133MP/2

     o   Best Performer, Multi-user/Shared System, $150,000 and 
         over: 

              AlphaServer 8400 5/350

     o   Best Throughput Performer, File Server Mix, $150,000 and 
         over: 

              AlphaServer 2100 5/300

     o   Best Throughput Performer, Multi-user/Shared System, 
         $50,000 to $149,000: 

     	       AlphaServer 2100 5/250

     o   Best Price/Performance Throughput, Multi-user/Shared 
         System, under $25,000: 

     	       Prioris XL Server 5100DP

     o   Best Price/Performance Throughput, File Server Mix, 
         $150,000 and over: 

     	       AlphaServer 2100 5/300

     o   Best Throughput Performer, File Server Mix, under 
         $25,000: 

     	       Prioris LX 5120

     o   Best Price/Performance Throughput, File Server Mix, under 
         $25,000: 

              Prioris LX 5120

     o   Best Throughput Performer, File Server Mix, $25,000 to 
         $49,000: 

              Prioris ZX 5133MP/2
         
     "Digital is indeed pleased that our systems continue to set 
the standard in the independent and highly regarded AIM 
benchmarks," said Mike Gallup, Digital vice president of 
worldwide systems marketing.  "Once again, the latest AIM 
results demonstrate that Alpha is the ideal UNIX platform for 
high-performance workstation, departmental, and enterprise 
server environments. Our customers, partners and channels 
continue to benefit from Digital's leadership in providing 
the industry's most powerful, expandable, affordable 
systems." 

     "This is the fourth consecutive time our Prioris PC servers 
have taken top honors from AIM. Winning five Hot Iron Awards 
is a clear validation of our product line's balanced system 
design, providing maximum server performance at PC price 
points," said Duane Dickhut, vice president of Digital's PC 
server product line. "Digital's commitment to world-class 
performance, reliability  and engineering excellence provides 
our customers an unequaled value proposition that enables 
them to reap maximum return for their technological 
investment."

     Since 1981, AIM Technology has provided vendors and end users 
comprehensive, unbiased performance testing to help users 
determine the best fit between their application needs and 
available systems and configurations. 

     AIM's service helps users reduce the costs of evaluating new 
systems and provides valuable broad-spectrum performance 
visibility for vendors that submit systems to be tested. AIM 
is an independent organization, as opposed to a vendor 
consortium, which enables AIM to bring an expert eye to 
performance measurement not restrained by objectives of 
consortium members. 

     Digital Equipment Corporation is the world's leader in open 
client/server solutions, from personal computing to 
integrated worldwide information systems. Digital's scalable 
Alpha platforms, storage, networking, software and services, 
together with industry-focused solutions from business 
partners, help organizations compete and win in today's 
global marketplace. 

     For more information, visit the Digital World Wide Web site 
at: www.digital.com
